{"_id":"68a736098ec3d8323af1134a","roadmapSlug":"android","nodeId":"yE0qAQZiEC9R8WvCdskpr","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:49.707Z","description":"# Column and Row in Compose\n\nColumn and Row are fundamental layout composables in Jetpack Compose used to arrange items vertically (Column) or horizontally (Row). They provide a simple and intuitive way to organize UI elements by stacking them in a single direction, offering control over how items are aligned and spaced within the layout. This makes creating responsive and visually appealing user interfaces much easier.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Column","url":"https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/Column.composable#Column(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Vertical,androidx.compose.ui.Alignment.Horizontal,kotlin.Function1)(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Vertical,androidx.compose.ui.Alignment.Horizontal,kotlin.Function1)","_id":"6a6330a80c2839ce78f8b258"},{"type":"official","title":"Row","url":"https://developer.android.com/reference/kotlin/androidx/compose/foundation/layout/Row.composable#Row(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Horizontal,androidx.compose.ui.Alignment.Vertical,kotlin.Function1)(androidx.compose.ui.Modifier,androidx.compose.foundation.layout.Arrangement.Horizontal,androidx.compose.ui.Alignment.Vertical,kotlin.Function1)","_id":"6a6330a80c2839ce78f8b259"}],"updatedAt":"2026-07-24T09:30:16.097Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/android/content/yE0qAQZiEC9R8WvCdskpr.md"}